WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome, welcome, welcome,
welcome to

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.167
"The Tonight Show," everyone.

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:04.667
You're here. You made it.

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:06.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.300
Thank you for being here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.767
Guys, let's get to some really,
really important news.

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:14.367
Yeah. I read that
due to a seed shortage,

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:16.901
mustard could be in short supply
this summer.

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:18.701
[ Audience murmurs ]
Yeah.

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:21.167
Luckily, every parent still has
a barrel in the fridge

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:23.100
that they bought from Costco
in 1997.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.100
[ Laughter ]
We're gonna be alright.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.901
That's right, a mustard shortage
is happening.

00:00:27.901 --> 00:00:31.100
Apparently, all supermarkets are
down to only 5,000 options.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:34.067
That's interesting.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.901
You can tell things are bad.

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:38.167
Today, President Biden called
Emmanuel Macron like,

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:40.701
"Pardon me, would you have
any Grey Poupon?"

00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:43.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:45.801
Yeah, there's a shortage of
mustard seeds.

00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:47.033
Then French's was like,

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:49.300
"Thank God we make ours
from plutonium, so..."

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:52.868
Did you guys hear about this?

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:56.267
Toyota is recalling all of their
new electric S.U.V.s because

00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:58.968
there's a risk that all --
the wheels are falling off

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:01.200
while being driven.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:07.133
Toyota told the owners, "Drop
off your car to be fixed."

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.067
And the owners are like, "Uh,
how about, can you come to us?

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:14.200
[ Laughter ]
"I mean, we have no wheels."

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.667
Right now, there's a Toyota
factory worker who's like,

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:19.767
"Oh, that's what those
50,000 bolts are for.

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:22.434
I'm an idiot. I'm sorry."

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:23.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:25.901
Guys, get this.
FedEx announced that they will

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:29.234
start taking photographs of
customers' packages to prove

00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:30.267
that they were delivered.

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:31.968
[ Audience ohs ]
Yeah.

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:33.334
In fact, they even released
this commercial.

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:34.634
Watch this.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:37.167
-We here at FedEx know
your packages are important,

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:39.067
so we're taking photographs
to prove

00:01:39.067 --> 00:01:41.167
they were delivered on time...

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:43.934
...when scheduled...

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:45.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:47.634
...and with the utmost care.

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:49.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.200
FedEx, nothin' but net.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:52.200
-There you go.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:56.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:56.601 --> 00:01:59.234
[ Cymbal crashes ]

00:01:59.234 --> 00:02:01.567
That last one had good aim.
-That last one was great.

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:03.300
-Yeah. Whoever that was
was good, yeah.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.467
Switching gears, there's
a new documentary coming out

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:09.334
about January 6th that has
exclusive interviews

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:10.834
with former president Trump,

00:02:10.834 --> 00:02:12.767
and they just released
the first footage.

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:14.467
Let's take a look.

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:21.200
-I don't think you want to have
the water in the picture, right?

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.901
You can take it out.
You know what you can do, Nick?

00:02:23.901 --> 00:02:26.334
Put the table back, and put the
water on the table

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:30.033
without the thing on top of it.

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:32.834
Go ahead. Take it out.

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:34.667
Yeah.

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:35.868
Alright.

00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:36.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.901 --> 00:02:38.434
Right, let's go.

00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:45.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:46.334
-Riveting.

00:02:46.334 --> 00:02:47.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:49.734
People were like, "Forget
January 6th, just give me

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:51.567
12 more hours of what happened
to that table."

00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:52.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:53.934
[ as Trump ]
The table isn't working.

00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:56.267
Get Rudy Giuliani to get on
all fours

00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:58.167
and then balance the water on
his head."

00:02:58.167 --> 00:03:00.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.267 --> 00:03:02.601
[ Normal voice ] As I mentioned
before, YouTube has

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:04.901
a new feature where you can skip
the boring parts of a video

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:06.400
and cut right to the good part.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:09.334
And I guess they have something
similar on TikTok as well.

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:11.767
We tried it out with some recent
videos people have posted.

00:03:11.767 --> 00:03:15.234
For instance, if you're watching
a video, you can skip this part.

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:18.067
-Whee!

00:03:18.067 --> 00:03:19.501
Whee!

00:03:19.501 --> 00:03:21.334
-Yeah. And go right to this.

00:03:22.734 --> 00:03:23.667
-Whe--

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:26.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:30.367
-Oh! Ow!

00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:32.167
-Let me give you
another example.

00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:33.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.534 --> 00:03:37.033
Let me give you another example.
You can skip this part.

00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:39.400
[ Bell tolls ]

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.167
[ Audience groans ]

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:43.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:46.000
And go right to this.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.000
[ Bell tolls ]

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.267
[ Audience ohs ]

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:51.067
She missed, she missed,
she missed.

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:53.334
Maybe one more final example.
-One more.

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:54.067
-Yeah, one example.

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.834
You can skip this part.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:58.334
[ Both scream ]

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:02.234
And go right to this.

00:04:02.234 --> 00:04:04.734
[ Both scream ]

00:04:04.734 --> 00:04:10.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:14.234
Swa-- Swallowed his necklace.

00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:16.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.968 --> 00:04:19.567
Going upside down.
Yeah, he swallowed his necklace.

00:04:19.567 --> 00:04:21.734
[ Imitates choking ]
Oh, man, he's good.

00:04:21.734 --> 00:04:23.033
He's alright.

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:25.300
Hey, guys, I saw that Netflix
officially confirmed

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.200
that they are going to add
a cheaper version

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.467
of their service that has ads.

00:04:29.467 --> 00:04:31.000
Yep.
[ Audience boos ]

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.934 --> 00:04:35.200
A cheaper Netflix with ads, yep.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.501
And they're going to
call it Hulu.

00:04:36.501 --> 00:04:40.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:42.934
Guys, listen to this.
Amazon just announced that

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:45.434
they're working on a new feature
that lets Alexa speak

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:47.167
in anyone's voice.
[ Audience oohs ]

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:48.968
You just give it
some reference audio,

00:04:48.968 --> 00:04:51.300
and then it can impersonate
your voice.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.601
I think it's pretty cool.
Let's check it out.

00:04:53.601 --> 00:04:56.300
Hey, Alexa.
-How can I help you?

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:59.534
-Alexa, speak to me in the voice
of Jimmy Fallon.

00:04:59.534 --> 00:05:02.934
-[ Masculine voice ] Okay.
Now, I am Jimmy Fallon.

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:06.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:08.701
-Sorry, that's your -- that's
your impression of me?

00:05:08.701 --> 00:05:12.033
-Yes. Hey, Guys.
I'm Jimmy Fallon.

00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:15.934
I host "The Tonight Show
Starring Jimmy Fallon."

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:17.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.734 --> 00:05:19.834
-That's not a very good
impression.

00:05:19.834 --> 00:05:22.601
-Wrong. I sound just like you.

00:05:22.601 --> 00:05:25.100
Everyone, give it up for
the Roots.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:30.300
-No, I d--
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.968
I do not sound like that.

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:34.767
-Yes, you do. I'm Jimmy Fallon.

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:36.868
My favorite place is my desk.

00:05:36.868 --> 00:05:39.100
I have a mug on my desk.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.734
I love my desk and my mug.

00:05:41.734 --> 00:05:44.300
-I mean, you do say that a lot.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.200
-I do not.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:49.067
-Higgins gets what I am
talking about.

00:05:49.067 --> 00:05:53.100
-Fine, Alexa, speak to me in
the voice of Steve Higgins.

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:55.033
-[ as Jimmy Fallon ] Hi, Jimmy.
It's me, Steve Higgins.

00:05:55.033 --> 00:05:56.434
How can I help you?

00:05:56.434 --> 00:05:58.334
-That -- That sounds
just like me.

00:05:58.334 --> 00:05:59.634
-[ Masculine voice ] No.

00:05:59.634 --> 00:06:02.267
That was my impression of
Steve Higgins.

00:06:02.267 --> 00:06:03.467
I'm Jimmy Fallon.

00:06:03.467 --> 00:06:04.767
-Okay, good, I think this needs
more work.

00:06:04.767 --> 00:06:06.367
Let's move on.

00:06:06.367 --> 00:06:10.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:10.234 --> 00:06:12.968
Some big sports news --
tonight was the NBA draft

00:06:12.968 --> 00:06:14.868
over at the Barclays Center
in Brooklyn.

00:06:14.868 --> 00:06:16.634
[ Audience cheers ]
Yeah, what a night.

00:06:16.634 --> 00:06:18.167
In 20 years, we'll be able to
look back

00:06:18.167 --> 00:06:20.334
and say that suit
did not age well.

00:06:20.334 --> 00:06:24.334
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.334 --> 00:06:26.000
The draft is exciting.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:29.100
For two hours, NBA commissioner
Adam Silver announces the picks

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:30.868
and then flies back
to his home planet.

00:06:30.868 --> 00:06:32.467
It's really -- It's great.

00:06:32.467 --> 00:06:35.501
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.501 --> 00:06:38.000
Seriously, you got to love
the NBA draft.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.901
It's the one night a year where
a 20-year-old genuinely says,

00:06:40.901 --> 00:06:42.801
"Yes, I get to move to
Sacramento."

00:06:42.801 --> 00:06:45.267
[ Laughter ]
Guys, well, this is wild.

00:06:45.267 --> 00:06:47.868
Guys, Billie Eilish revealed
that she sent a body double

00:06:47.868 --> 00:06:51.100
out on stage in her place at
the start of her Coachella set,

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:52.667
and no one noticed.

00:06:52.667 --> 00:06:54.501
That's pretty crazy.
Right, Tariq?

00:06:54.501 --> 00:06:57.367
-Yeah, Jimmy.
That's some pretty wild stuff.

00:06:57.367 --> 00:07:02.067
[ Laughter ]

00:07:02.067 --> 00:07:04.901
-Higgins, notice anything
different about Tariq?

00:07:04.901 --> 00:07:08.033
-Uh, no. Looks like the same old
Tariq to me, Jimmy.

00:07:08.033 --> 00:07:09.367
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.367 --> 00:07:12.300
-Quest, I think some people are
using body doubles.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:15.100
-Yeah, I mean, that's kind of
unprofessional.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.501
You're right. Yeah.

00:07:16.501 --> 00:07:18.133
-I agree. Well.

00:07:18.133 --> 00:07:19.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:19.534 --> 00:07:23.334
In other news...
[ Applause ]

00:07:23.334 --> 00:07:26.133
...I saw that a Swedish man
broke a world record

00:07:26.133 --> 00:07:29.300
by throwing a washing machine
more than 14 feet.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:32.834
Yeah, the name of the record he
broke was World's Weirdest Man.

00:07:32.834 --> 00:07:37.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:39.501
-That's the stuff!

00:07:39.501 --> 00:07:41.968
That's the stuff right there,
Fallon!

00:07:41.968 --> 00:07:46.467
[ Laughter ]

00:07:46.467 --> 00:07:48.434
-Calm down, sir.
-Where'd he get the popcorn?

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:51.601
-I don't know.
He's not even wearing a mask.

00:07:51.601 --> 00:07:52.701
-[ Laughing ]
He's not wearing a mask.

00:07:52.701 --> 00:07:54.100
-Sir, please calm down.

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:55.667
"That's the stuff"?
-That's the stuff, man.

00:07:55.667 --> 00:07:57.567
Come on, that's the stuff.

00:07:57.567 --> 00:08:01.400
-Guys, I read there's
a rail-worker strike

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:04.501
in the U.K. right now,
and one man who always rides

00:08:04.501 --> 00:08:05.901
the train has beaten the strike

00:08:05.901 --> 00:08:08.367
by paddling to work in
an inflatable kayak.

00:08:08.367 --> 00:08:09.534
Here he is.

00:08:09.534 --> 00:08:11.200
Yeah.

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:13.133
If you thought the guy who biked
to work was insufferable,

00:08:13.133 --> 00:08:14.267
imagine this guy.

00:08:14.267 --> 00:08:15.567
[ Laughter ]

00:08:15.567 --> 00:08:16.667
Hey, this is fun, guys.

00:08:16.667 --> 00:08:19.634
A Star Wars fan just spent
$2.3 million

00:08:19.634 --> 00:08:22.167
on a model of an X-Wing fighter.

00:08:22.167 --> 00:08:23.834
Yeah, when the buyer told
his wife, she said,

00:08:23.834 --> 00:08:25.501
"Congrats, you now have
two exes."

00:08:25.501 --> 00:08:29.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:29.133 --> 00:08:33.167
-Come on, that's the stuff.

00:08:33.167 --> 00:08:35.434
Fore!

00:08:35.434 --> 00:08:37.968
-Finally
"Thor: Love and Thunder"

00:08:37.968 --> 00:08:39.067
is almost in theaters.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:39.067 --> 00:08:41.200
I know.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:46.267
I'm excited.

00:08:46.267 --> 00:08:48.801
And ahead of the release,
we thought that we'd share

00:08:48.801 --> 00:08:51.901
some fun facts about Marvel's
famous God of Thunder.

00:08:51.901 --> 00:08:54.601
This is
"Thor: Little Known Facts."

00:08:54.601 --> 00:08:55.934
-♪ Thor ♪

00:08:55.934 --> 00:08:59.434
♪ Little known facts ♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:59.434 --> 00:09:01.501
But first, I'm going to need
someone to help me.

00:09:01.501 --> 00:09:03.400
His new movie
"Thor: Love and Thunder"

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:07.133
is in theaters on July 8th.
Please welcome Chris Hemsworth.

00:09:07.133 --> 00:09:11.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:11.868 --> 00:09:15.167
-Hello.
-Chris!

00:09:15.167 --> 00:09:17.467
-How you doing?
-How are you, bud?

00:09:17.467 --> 00:09:19.501
-I'm very well, mate. Very well.

00:09:19.501 --> 00:09:20.801
-Thank you so much
for doing this.

00:09:20.801 --> 00:09:23.133
Chris, our researchers found
some interesting facts

00:09:23.133 --> 00:09:26.834
about Thor to help fans get
ready for the big premiere.

00:09:26.834 --> 00:09:28.067
-Of course they did, Jimmy.

00:09:28.067 --> 00:09:30.367
I was very impressed with what
you guys found.

00:09:30.367 --> 00:09:33.234
This stuff -- it's stuff that I
didn't even know.

00:09:33.234 --> 00:09:36.934
Only hard-core comic book fans
do, so it's very exciting.

00:09:36.934 --> 00:09:38.567
-I think our research team
did a great job.

00:09:38.567 --> 00:09:40.801
Let's get started with some
little-know facts about Thor.

00:09:40.801 --> 00:09:42.267
Here we go, I'll go first.

00:09:42.267 --> 00:09:44.934
Did you know that Thor's father
is Odin, but his godfather

00:09:44.934 --> 00:09:47.367
is actually
Sean "P. Diddy" Combs.

00:09:47.367 --> 00:09:48.834
[ Laughter ]

00:09:48.834 --> 00:09:50.701
-It's true. It's true.

00:09:50.701 --> 00:09:52.167
It's actually the plot
of this film.

00:09:52.167 --> 00:09:53.667
So we shouldn't say too much
about it.

00:09:53.667 --> 00:09:56.968
-No spoilers, yeah.
Why don't you give me one?

00:09:56.968 --> 00:09:59.300
-Asgardians prolong their lives
by eating

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:01.200
the Golden Apples of Idunn.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:06.434
The Asgardians learned of the
apples in an article on Goop.

00:10:06.434 --> 00:10:09.868
-Wow.
I didn't know they had Goop.

00:10:09.868 --> 00:10:12.901
-Gwyneth Paltrow linked it.
-Yeah, I love those articles.

00:10:12.901 --> 00:10:14.200
How about this one?

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:18.200
Thor's full name is actually
Courtney Thorne Smith.

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:20.033
Did you know that?
-Can you believe it?

00:10:20.033 --> 00:10:22.968
-Yeah.
These are all fascinating.

00:10:22.968 --> 00:10:26.167
-In this one, Thor has to get a
job because he lost all of his

00:10:26.167 --> 00:10:30.300
money on "Thored Ape" NFTs.
-Oh, it's tough.

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:33.267
-He's a big metaverse guy.
-It's a tough market right now.

00:10:33.267 --> 00:10:35.300
How about this one?
Everyone knows Chris Hemsworth's

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:38.033
brothers Liam and Luke,
but he also has a fourth brother

00:10:38.033 --> 00:10:39.634
named Clemsworth Hemsworth.

00:10:39.634 --> 00:10:41.601
He plays bass with
the Jonas Brothers.

00:10:41.601 --> 00:10:43.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:43.834 --> 00:10:46.367
-Clemsworth, he's a guy.
-He's good.

00:10:46.367 --> 00:10:47.834
Talented, talented,
talented guy.

00:10:47.834 --> 00:10:51.300
Why don't you give me one?
-Thor's hammer is named Mjolnir.

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:54.100
His belt is named is Megingjord.

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:56.067
And his pecks are named
Bert and Ernie.

00:10:56.067 --> 00:10:57.534
[ Laughter and applause ]
-There you go.

00:10:57.534 --> 00:10:59.567
